        "title": "Gemstones - Classification, Crystal Systems, the 4Cs",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "ALL GEMSTONES\n├── MINERALS (crystalline inorganic solids — most gems)\n│   ├── Native elements\n│   │   └── Diamond (C, cubic, sp³ covalent bonds, hardness 10)\n│   ├── Oxides\n│   │   ├── Corundum (Al₂O₃, trigonal) → ruby (Cr³⁺), sapphire (Fe²⁺/Ti⁴⁺)\n│   │   └── Spinel (MgAl₂O₄) — often mistaken for ruby historically\n│   ├── Silicates (Si-O backbone, most gem species)\n│   │   ├── Cyclosilicates\n│   │   │   ├── Beryl (Be₃Al₂Si₆O₁₈) → emerald (Cr), aquamarine (Fe)\n│   │   │   └── Tourmaline (complex borosilicate) — widest color range\n│   │   ├── Nesosilicates\n│   │   │   ├── Garnet group (pyrope, almandine, spessartine, grossular,\n│   │   │   │    andradite demantoid, uvarovite tsavorite)\n│   │   │   └── Topaz (Al₂SiO₄(F,OH)₂)\n│   │   ├── Inosilicates\n│   │   │   └── Jadeite (NaAlSi₂O₆) — \"true jade\"\n│   │   └── Tectosilicates\n│   │       ├── Quartz (SiO₂) → amethyst, citrine, rose quartz\n│   │       └── Feldspar → moonstone, labradorite\n│   ├── Phosphates\n│   │   └── Turquoise (CuAl₆(PO₄)₄(OH)₈·4H₂O)\n│   └── Sulfates / Carbonates\n│       └── Malachite (Cu₂(CO₃)(OH)₂)\n├── ROCKS (polycrystalline / multi-mineral aggregates)\n│   └── Lapis lazuli (lazurite + pyrite + calcite)\n└── ORGANICS (biogenic materials)\n    ├── Pearl (nacre: CaCO₃ aragonite + conchiolin protein)\n    ├── Amber (fossilized tree resin — polymerized terpenes)\n    ├── Coral (CaCO₃ calcite/aragonite)\n    └── Jet (fossilized wood — lignite coal)\n```"
    },
